{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":45},"timestamp":1790173321,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":".venv/bin/cortex-ask --real --tenant █████████ \"which acquisition ██████ produces deals that actually close, not just deals that get created?\"","title":"real_██████_quality","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: which acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 produces deals that actually close, not just deals that get created?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-23 19:52:02\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [ 12.1s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [ 12.1s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [ 17.3s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 24.7s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 24.7s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 26.5s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (2 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 26.5s] step 1   got hubspot__search (3 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 26.5s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 32.4s] step 2   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 32.4s] step 2   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 32.4s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588\u2588 rows) (3 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 34.4s] step 2   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 34.4s] step 2   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 34.4s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 45.1s] step 3   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 45.1s] step 3   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588\u2588 rows) (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 45.1s] step 3   ! hubspot__search failed: InvalidParams: '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' is not a filterable property of deals. Available: amount, closedate, createdate, dealname, dealstage, dealtype, hs_analytics_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, hs_analytics_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  [ 45.1s] step 4   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 83.0s]          drafting the report from 5 observation(s)\r\n  [127.5s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [127.5s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (4.2s); missing: Per-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 breakdown of closed-won deals with \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 field populated (most records show \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: null); Per-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 breakdown of closed-lost/created deals to compute win rate by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588; A \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-attribution audit explaining why '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' is null on the vast majority of records, since without it no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-to-close-rate comparison is possible\r\n  sufficiency gate withheld 1 causal claim(s)\r\n  [144.5s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Which acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 produces deals that actually close, not just deals that get created?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 127s over 4 steps, 70,906 tokens, 5 observations gathered, 3 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Acquisition-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 data on deals is \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ly missing (roughly two-thirds of sampled deals have no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 recorded), so a channel-quality ranking can only be built from the minority of deals that do carry a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 value.  [hubspot.search 30f5c1a8, hubspot.search 67a0a969]\r\n  Among deals with a recorded \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, OFFLINE (mostly sub-type IMPORT) produces both the most closed-won deals (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d wins, about $\u2588.\u2588M) and the most closed-lost deals (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 sampled losses), making it the dominant channel by volume but only a roughly \u2588\u2588% win rate among \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d deals.  [hubspot.search 23f34747, hubspot.search 67a0a969]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] ORGANIC_SEARCH is a materially better-closing acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 than OFFLINE/IMPORT.\r\n      Only one ORGANIC_SEARCH deal appears in either the closed-won or closed-lost samples pulled (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 Committee, won). A single data point cannot establish a channel's close rate; this is a count too small to rank against OFFLINE's dozens of observations, not evidence the channel performs better.\r\n  [inconclusive] OFFLINE (specifically the IMPORT sub-detail) is the acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 that most reliably produces deals which actually close, because it accounts for both the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st volume and dollar amount of closed-won deals among records where \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 is known.\r\n      Among the deals that actually carry a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 value, OFFLINE/IMPORT is both the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st contributor to closed-won (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d wins, ~$\u2588.\u2588M) and the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st contributor to closed-lost (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 sampled losses), meaning it is simply the dominant channel by volume, not necessarily the highest-quality one on a rate basis; its true win rate among \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d deals is far lower (~\u2588\u2588%) than its win count alone suggests.\r\n  [contradicted] The `\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588` field is a reliable proxy for true marketing/acquisition channel and can be used to rank channels by close quality.\r\n      A majority of deals created in the sampled window carry no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 value at all (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588), and a bulk-import batch on 2026-01-05 created \u2588\u2588+ records simultaneously with `\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588` null for most, which looks like a backfill/migration artifact rather than a marketing-channel record. hs_analytics_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, the field HubSpot itself \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ates for original-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 attribution, could not even be queried directly as a filter. This makes the `\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588` field too sparse and too contaminated by migration noise to support a confident channel-quality ranking.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Do not use the current `\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588`/`\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail` deal properties to make channel-investment decisions until data hygiene is fixed; instead, prioritize backfilling or correctly mapping hs_analytics_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 across the ~\u2588\u2588% of deals that currently have no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 recorded.\r\n      why: With two-thirds of deals un\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d and the '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' field appearing contaminated by a January bulk-import event, any channel ranking drawn from it \u2014 including the OFFLINE/IMPORT lead reported here \u2014 is likely an artifact of which records happen to carry a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 value rather than a true measure of channel quality.\r\n      [hubspot.search 30f5c1a8, hubspot.search 67a0a969]\r\n  P\u2588 Once \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 data is reliable, compute close rate (won / (won+lost)) per channel rather than raw win counts, since OFFLINE currently looks dominant only because it has the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st volume in both the won and lost buckets.\r\n      why: OFFLINE/IMPORT's \u2588\u2588 wins came with \u2588\u2588 losses among \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588d deals (\u2248\u2588\u2588% win rate), while its raw win count makes it look like the top channel purely due to volume; a rate-based view is needed before recommending budget shifts toward it.\r\n      [hubspot.search 23f34747, hubspot.search 67a0a969]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Over two-thirds of deal records lack any acquisition-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 value, so any ranking of channels by close rate is built on a minority, non-random subset of the pipeline (likely biased toward deals entered manually or via specific integrations rather than reflecting true traffic mix).\r\n  - The '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' property returned by search is a legacy/simplified field; HubSpot's true multi-touch attribution field (hs_analytics_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) was not accessible via this filter interface, so channel names used here (OFFLINE, ORGANIC_SEARCH) may not match the tenant's actual marketing-channel taxonomy.\r\n  - Closed-lost and created-deal totals were sampled (\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 respectively); the digests are exhaustive over the sample retrieved but not over the full population, so exact channel-level win rates could shift with the remaining untruncated rows.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The sampled records show most deals have null \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (only a few OFFLINE) supporting missing \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 data broadly, but no aggregate count confirms the precise 'roughly two-thirds' f\r\n- executive_summary[1]: The evidence shows OFFLINE/IMPORT deals appearing among both wins and losses, but the truncated payloads don't let us verify the specific counts (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588) or the $\u2588.\u2588M/\r\n- executive_summary[3]: asked as an open question, with this claim withheld, the same evidence does not establish a cause: This is a raw list of deals created in \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 with stage, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, and owner fields \r\n  - \u2588 causal claim(s) were withheld: a separate check of the evidence gathered, made without seeing this report, found that it does not support a definitive answer about cause. These observations show raw counts of closed-won and closed-lost deals and total created deals, but almost all records have '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' null, so there is no way to attribute closes to acquisition \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s. The data describes outcomes, not the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-level comparison the question requires. What would settle it: Per-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 breakdown of closed-won deals with \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 field populated (most records show \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: null); Per-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 breakdown of closed-lost/created deals to compute win rate by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588; A \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-attribution audit explaining why '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' is null on the vast majority of records, since without it no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-to-close-rate comparison is possible. What remains describes what happened, and stops short of why.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Deal `\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588`/`\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail` fields are null for the majority of both closed-won and closed-lost deals sampled, and a \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 cluster of records was created in a single bulk-import burst on 2026-01-05, which appears to be a data migration rather than organic deal creation \u2014 this limits any channel-level conclusion to the minority subset that has \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 populated.\r\n  - The closed-lost (\u2588\u2588\u2588 total) and all-deals-created (\u2588\u2588\u2588 total) searches were each truncated to \u2588\u2588\u2588 returned rows; digests cover all rows in the returned page but not the full population.\r\n  - The `\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588` property could not be used as a search filter directly ('\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' is not a filterable property of deals); only hs_analytics_\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and related fields are, but those were not explored, so this report relies on the `\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588` value embedded in returned deal records rather than a filtered query on it.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  30f5c1a8  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?createdate=2026-01-01..2026-09-23\r\n  23f34747  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  67a0a969  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (144s wall, 142s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1     12.0    8%    12.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      5.2    4%     5.2  in 0 out 0\r\n  loop_model       4     61.8   43%    15.5  in 8 out 5,092 cached 63,083\r\n  loop_tools       3      3.9    3%     1.3  in 0 out 0\r\n  draft            1     44.4   31%    44.4  in 61,790 out 4,016\r\n  gate             1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  verify           1     10.8    7%    10.8  in 47,216 out 1,359\r\n  sufficiency      1      4.2    3%     4.2  in 4,024 out 205\r\n  unmeasured              2.0    1%\r\n  cache hit rate: 36%\r\n"]
